Z||000013||FieroGTGirl||06-21-2000||12:13 AM||||87FeiroGT~~~~~<P>Great looking Feiro!!! I really like your wheels and that Pegasus on the rear window. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/cool.gif"><P>Is the red car a Grand Am or Grand Prix?  is it yours? If so what year?  And do you like it?<P>Reason I am asking is I am thinking about getting either a  2000 Grand Am or a 2000 Grand Prix... I want the two door like in your pics...<P>Thanks,<BR>Kristina||||reg||1
Z||000014||86SE||06-21-2000||12:44 AM||||What kind of yellow is that?? Is it GM yellow??  The reason I ask is because next month my Fiero will be painted Ferrari's Modena yellow.  The Ferrari yellow looks close to that but much brighter.||||reg||14
Z||000015||87FieroGT||06-21-2000||01:00 AM||||It is a custom yellow that I picked off a picture of a custom hodrod that was hanging on the wall at the paint store.  It became really custom when the guy mixed the paint because the paint code for the color was for Dupont ChromaBase but I went with Dupont Nason instead which is a cheaper paint. The Nason paint does not have a color code for the color so the guy matched the paint perfectly.  The difference in the paints is that the Nason is much thinner than the ChromaBase.  Hope this helped.  If you want the paint code for the ChromaBase I can get it for you.||||reg||6
Z||000016||mbramble||06-21-2000||08:30 AM||||Just out of curiosity, and if you don't mind saying -- how much did the paint cost you?  How much did you use??  Is there a clearcoat??  If so, how much used, and the cost???<P>Thanks,<BR>Mike<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000017||CUTTER||06-21-2000||05:52 PM||||How long did it take you to take all the panels off, paint them , and put them back on?<BR>Shane, 87GTblue  <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000018||87FieroGT||06-22-2000||02:26 AM||||MBRamble,  It cost me about $300 dollars for the paint and all the misc materials I needed.  The paint itseld was only $200 which came with a gallon of paint and a gallon of clear coat.  I had to also use a primer/sealer for the first coat which was an extra $40, but it was white and then tinted with yellow to make the color look better.  As far as the time it took me to do everything I don't have an exact hour count because I wasn't worried about and I just wanted to finish it right.  I would say that it took about 2 weeks, but that was because I had to do a lot of it after work.  Hope this helps you guys.||||reg||10
